+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered with `ToolRegistry` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` (`src/types/ai.ts`) that is forwarded to the AI provider and enforced by `ToolRegistry.execute` (`src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts`) before the tool's executor runs. Returning a rejection `ToolResponse` rather than throwing lets the model read what failed and correct its call within the tool-round budget, while throwing remains reserved for an unknown tool name.
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- Registering a static `ToolDefinition` compiles its `inputSchema` once at registration time, throwing synchronously with a message naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool for an invalid schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L13)).
+- A static tool's compiled validator is reused across `execute` calls rather than recompiled on each invocation.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves on each call and validates against the schema returned at that call rather than a stale registration-time schema ([validated by: validates each call against a function-valued definition current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L98)).
+
+## Input validation and failure modes
+
+- Before invoking the executor, `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against `required`, declared types, and `enum` only — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying defaults — and on failure returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing property paths and constraints while omitting every property value from both `result` and logs ([validated by: rejects invalid input with path and constraint without leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L28)).
+- Calling `execute` for an unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` rather than returning a `ToolResponse`, keeping a missing registration distinct from malformed model input.
+- In the orchestrator tool loop (`src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts`), a schema rejection reaches the provider as a `tool_result` message on the next round, and a corrected retry — including unlisted extra properties and omitted optional fields that carry a schema `default` — reaches the executor unchanged ([validated by: returns schema rejections to the model and passes valid retries unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L138)).
